                                          Printer not working


Initial Troubleshooting:

          Issue
Users are unable to print documents or print jobs that fail to complete.

          Steps
Verify the printer is powered on and properly connected.
Confirm the correct printer is set as the default printer.
Check the print queue for paused or stuck print jobs.
Restart the application and attempt to print again.



Devices and Printers window
(Shows where printers, status, and default printers are managed.) qqqq - how/commands -qqq


System-Level Troubleshooting

Steps:
- Open Services (services.msc).
Locate the Print Spooler service; it  handles interaction with the printer
Restart the Print Spooler to clear stuck print jobs.



[ Screenshot1]


Open Device Manager and verify printer driver status.
Inside Device Manager, my printer header appears under Print queues. This is because if no printer is connected, this section may appear empty, but it is the location to verify printer driver status




[ Screenshot2]

Shows previously connected printers and driver information. If a printer were connected, it would appear here with current driver and connection details.
Update or reinstall the printer driver if necessary.



